      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Catalyst::Plugin::Statsd versions through 0.10.0 for Perl may leak session ids.  If the communication channel to the statsd daemon is not secured (for example, by sending UDP packets to a host on another network), then users' session ids may be leaked.  This may allow an attacker to use session ids as authentication tokens.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
